.TH PACPANTOP 1 "May 2026" "pacpantop" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pacpantop \- lightweight TTY LAN monitor for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pacpantop
.RI [ subnet-prefix ]
.br
.B pacpantop --beep-test
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pacpantop
scans a local /24 network, reads the local neighbor table, tracks visible devices,
and displays device state in a terminal interface.
.PP
It is intended for low-resource TTY machines that stay on as simple LAN warning
monitors. It can beep when device state changes and can optionally fetch extra
system information from reachable Linux devices through SSH.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I subnet-prefix
First three octets of the /24 subnet to scan. Example: 10.0.0 scans
10.0.0.1 through 10.0.0.254.
.SH DISPLAY
.TP
.B Host box
Shows the monitor name, host, online device count, scan interval, time, uptime,
and subnet.
.TP
.B Devices box
Shows IP, MAC, known name, status, and uptime for visible or remembered devices.
.TP
.B Host System panel
Shows local OS, architecture, kernel, uptime, and OS age.
.TP
.B Network Fetch panel
Shows optional SSH/fallback information for selected reachable Linux devices.
.SH STATUS VALUES
.TP
.B online
The device is visible and authorized or already known.
.TP
.B offline
The device is remembered but not currently visible.
.TP
.B pending
The device needs authorization.
.TP
.B blocked
The device was blocked by the user.
.SH SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B a
Authorize the first pending or unknown visible device. If it has no name,
pacpantop asks for a custom name.
.TP
.B b
Block the first unknown visible device.
.TP
.B r
Reset the display state and fetch cache. This does not delete known devices,
authorized MACs, or blocked-device history.
.TP
.B m
Open this manual page when available.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Quit pacpantop.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/lan-known-devices.txt
Saved local device names.
.TP
.I ~/lan-authorized-macs.txt
Authorized MAC addresses.
.TP
.I ~/lan-blocked-devices.txt
Blocked-device log.
.TP
.I ~/lan-ssh-users.txt
Optional SSH usernames for remote fetches.
.TP
.I ~/lan-online-since.txt
Online duration tracking state.
.SH NOTES
Private LAN data files should not be published.
.SH AUTHOR
Pacpan
